  "summary": "A regionalized modular access ecosystem in which a vendor-aware dropper (key derived from SHA1(\"ShareTech\")) writes a .php shell script to a storage mount, stages AVERAT and BPFDoor/Rekoobe payloads into /sbin as ntpdate/udevds, launches them and unlinks them so /proc/<pid>/exe reads (deleted). AVERAT beacons over outbound SMTP port 25 with a hand-built TLS ClientHello and a 276-byte encrypted config, while BPFDoor and Rekoobe variants sit passive on raw PF_PACKET sockets behind classic BPF filters gated on per-sample magic bytes and passwords. Defense should focus on unlinked process images, unexpected port-25 callbacks, raw/BPF socket creation, appliance staging paths and process masquerading.",
